## B. THE LIST — in this order

### 1. Node-20 GitHub Actions fix
One deploy already failed; every later item ships through this pipeline.
Bump `actions/checkout` and `actions/upload-artifact` versions in the workflow.
Smallest item, largest blast radius. Repo-side only, no index.html change.

### 2. Live sync test protocol
Answers "does sync work perfectly?" with evidence instead of memory.
Scripted two-device run: fresh key → study on A → open B → max-merge check →
off/on re-key flow → beacon-on-close check. Findings become list items; no
code until tested. (Code inspection alone cannot prove sync correctness.)

### 3. Pre-adoption warning dialog (key-collision)
The one real sync-safety gap: entering a key on a device that already has
progress merges irreversibly, silently (max only knows up).
Split syncPull into look-fetch + apply; new sync-panel state `key-collision`
with three doors: Take the cloud / Merge / Cancel. NOT built — grep confirms
no such state exists.

### 4. About & copy sweep (docs-in-app)
Three approved sentences still missing from the app:
- server-limit ("…syncing stops until the next day. Your scores stay in your browser.")
- sync promise ("Your progress follows your devices — sometimes a device
  catches up when you next open it.") — not "always in sync"
- honest "Turn off sync" label (it disconnects this device; deletes nothing) — R1.3
Small, pure copy, zero risk.

### 5. Self-host SheetJS + precache converter.html
index.html line 1235 still loads SheetJS from cdnjs — the last third-party
runtime dependency, inconsistent with the self-hosted-Poppins principle.
Vendor the file into the repo, point both index.html and converter.html at it,
precache. Enables true offline Excel import.

### 6. Mobile pass + rail zone reorder (bundled — same screen region)
6a. Verify/fix rail footer (Info · Scores · Settings) reachability on mobile —
the suspected real blocker to sharing the app. Only 3 media queries exist;
needs live phone test first.
6b. Michel's flag: domain zones (ACTIVE / MY LISTS / MORE) to be reordered.
NEEDS MICHEL'S SPEC: target order and reasoning, decided at the start of this item.

### 7. Profiles (WD_Bouwplan_Profielen.md)
Decided 2026-08-28, fully designed, zero server cost. The biggest build on the
list: local profiles for shared devices (the classroom scenario), sync under
profiles, the lazy rule. Four open design questions in the Bouwplan to settle
first — design session, then build sessions.

### 8. R3 decision: push on large delta
Decide, don't drift: does deck-completion push when the brake is open, or does
the three-condition rule stay pure? One session, outcome is either "build it"
